# Review

The note passes the marginal-value test. Each chunk has its own job. Stakes sets the scope gap, the cost pressure, and the retirement condition for the standing query. Current answer gives five distinct lenses, and each lens adds a different selection signal with its own link. Unsettled names four separate gaps: root versus sub-question value propagation, asymmetric selection pressure, cold-start admission, and combining signals. None of these gaps restates a lens without adding something new.

The "Similarly" sentence in the validity bullet is not redundant. It brings in fit within a working theory, which differs from earned maintenance cost. The parenthetical list of signals in the last Unsettled bullet is also not redundant: it names the dimensions to be combined, including two that the lenses do not cover (demand-root coverage and maintenance cost). The Relevant Notes footer repeats links from the body, but it follows the collection's link-labeling convention, so I did not flag it.

The one uncertain spot is the closing clause of the asymmetric-selection bullet. It partly repeats the clutter consequence from Stakes. I logged it as info, not warn, because its condition about fluent local additions may be doing explanatory work.
